-- title:
--   Component-swapping endomorphism of the 𝔽ₚ-fibre of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$, assumed nonzero, have image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of the $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); finally $\mathbb{Z}/p$ is given as an $A$-algebra. Then the fibre product of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) (the structure morphism of the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebras generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$) with $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}/p) \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ admits an endomorphism $\tau$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}/p)$, i.e. $\tau$ followed by the second projection equals the second projection, such that every irreducible component $Z$ of the underlying space of this fibre product is mapped by the continuous map underlying $\tau$ into some irreducible component $Z' \neq Z$.
--
--   This realises, on the mod $p$ fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$, the level-$p$ Atkin–Lehner involution, whose effect on the two components of the fibre (the two Igusa-type components in the Deligne–Rapoport description) is to interchange them. It is used in the construction of a point on each component: knowing that the reduction of the cusp $\infty$ lies on one component, its image under $\tau$ lies on the other.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_hom_pullback_snd_forall_exists_ne_mapsTo_irreducibleComponents_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

